.TH "GF-DATASOURCES-QUERY-METRICS-WITH-EXPRESSIONS" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-datasources-query-metrics-with-expressions - Data source query metrics with expressions


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf datasources query-metrics-with-expressions [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Data source query metrics with expressions

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled you need to have a permission with action: \fBdatasources:query\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (MetricRequest):
{
  "debug": boolean,
  "from": string,
  "queries": [any],
  "to": string
}
  from                     required
  queries                  required
  to                       required


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	The path to the body json file or json string. For example, --body=/path/to/body.json or --body='{"foo": "bar"}'

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for query-metrics-with-expressions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-datasources(1)\fP
